// the action table: one line per action with its args; keep it equal to the dispatch in K.serve and K.more
// prompt: the text of the actions action: every action Kernel.serve and Kernel.more dispatch, one line each, with its args and rules.
def Kernel.acts(): Str = "actions\nshow NAME..\nfind TEXT   (names of the units whose text contains TEXT)\nids   (units, edges, sccs, ties; then name and identity: no name is hashed, a rename keeps every id; the store writes the same text to DIR/IDS)\nprompts   (units, and units without a `// prompt:` line)\ntype SIG   (names of the def/val units whose telescope and result type equal SIG; binder names and spaces do not count)\nedit NAME<NL>OLD<NL>===<NL>NEW   (OLD must occur exactly once in the unit; the result goes through the gate)\ncycle DIR OUT.c BIN   (store DIR, build OUT.c, cc OUT.c BIN)\nlist\nsubmit<NL>TEXT   (every new or changed unit of submit, edit and ingest must hold a line `// prompt: TEXT` stating its behaviour, else error[prompt-missing])\ntests   (every test val NAME {Test}: Test.Result = Test.expect(got, want, \"why\"), computed natively: NAME ok, or NAME FAIL: expected W, found G: why)\nnegtests   (each NegTest val NAME {NegTest}: Never = with an indented body of top-level decls and a last line NegTest.expect(\"code\", .., \"why\"): ok when the kernel rejects the body with exactly those codes; the report gives the reason)\ndrop NAME..   (remove the units; the result goes through the gate; a name of no unit rejects all)\ncheck<NL>TEXT\ningest PATH..\nload DIR P..   (the units of the tree DIR (X.Y.z in DIR/X/Y/z.srs), only those under the prefixes P.. when given)\nstore DIR P..   (the image as a tree, only the units under the prefixes P.. when given, and DIR/IDS)\nbuild OUT.c\ncc IN.c OUT\nrelaunch BIN\nstop\nnegrun BASE LIST\nfacts BASE FILE\ngate BASE FILE\nplan DL DIR OUT\ndlrun DL DIR OUT\nhashfile PATH..\nrenamestore SRC DST OLD NEW\n"

